the set of homotopy classes is just the cohomology group Hqk+1+1(X (k−1); πk+1).39 The classes
are known as Postnikov invariants. For a π-finite space, the tower will terminate at some
finite stage. The full tower X has jth homotopy group πj. If all the Postnikov invariants
vanish then X is just �

j K(πj, qj). Otherwise, it is a twisted product of Eilenberg-MacLane
spaces, and in general is not homotopy equivalent to a direct product of Eilenberg-MacLane
spaces.40

As the simplest nontrivial example, a 2-stage Postnikov decomposition of the form

K(A, 2)
