## Batch 14 authoring complete

Authored the A/B pages and five assigned items: the finite background gauging definition, weighted gluing theorem, and three finite examples. The pages have YAML frontmatter only. Updated the batch manifest, proof contracts, coverage, cross-batch dependency rows, notes, and Step 1 records.

The scoped checks passed: proof layout (5 items, 19 steps), proof contracts, precheck, rendering, content policy, manifest dependencies, focused dependency closure, coverage, source stamps, and the final claim-to-manifest and empty-page checks.

## Open prerequisite

All five Step 1 records are **escalated**. The page-13 consistency proof has an unexpanded coherence argument at step 2.2, and its gauge-label automorphism convention is unresolved. The generic finite-groupoid proofs remain conditional and do not claim the two-group instance is proved. The required page-13 dependency is recorded as open in the [cross-batch dependency file](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library-aqft-20261023/physics/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.cross-batch-dependencies.json).

The batch-14 dependency row still recomputes to level 1 with prerequisite batch 13. The shared dependency-level digest is stale after run-manifest changes; I left that owner-controlled file unchanged. The [batch notes](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library-aqft-20261023/physics/research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md) record the source locators and stamps, item levels, check results, record hashes, and prerequisite gap.

